1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,093
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,093 --> 00:00:03,400
I'd like to open a bank account, please.

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:03,450
Certainly.

4
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:08,162
If you'd like to take a seat, I'll just get some details from you.

5
00:00:08,162 --> 00:00:09,432
It won't take long.

6
00:00:09,432 --> 00:00:09,750
Thanks.

7
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:14,032
Is it a current account or a deposit account you wanted?

8
00:00:14,032 --> 00:00:15,200
A current account.

9
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:15,653
Right.

10
00:00:15,653 --> 00:00:18,827
I've got the application form here then.

11
00:00:18,827 --> 00:00:23,360
We have different types-I see you've got our leaflet there.

12
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,920
I've decided on the one called 'Select.'

13
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:26,249
Right,

14
00:00:26,249 --> 00:00:26,908
that's fine,

15
00:00:26,908 --> 00:00:30,530
so, first of all, can I have your full name please?

16
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:34,077
Yes, it's Pieter Henes.

17
00:00:34,077 --> 00:00:35,850
That's P-I-E-T-E-R.

18
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,600
Is it H-E-double N-E-S?

19
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,138
Uh, only one N actually.

20
00:00:40,138 --> 00:00:42,600
It's a less common spelling of the name.

21
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,462
Oh, right.

22
00:00:43,462 --> 00:00:43,893
OK.

23
00:00:43,893 --> 00:00:46,910
And what's your date of birth please?

24
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:50,600
The twenty-seventh of the first, nineteen seventy-three.

25
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:51,079
Right.

26
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:54,433
And will this be a joint account?

27
00:00:54,433 --> 00:00:55,870
No, just myself.

28
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:56,930
OK, fine.

29
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:00,110
And where are you living, Mr.

30
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:00,640
Henes?

31
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:01,170
15.

32
00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:01,700
Riverside.

33
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,325
Is that all one word?

34
00:01:04,325 --> 00:01:04,850
Yes.

35
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:05,375
Exeter?

36
00:01:05,375 --> 00:01:05,900
Yes.

37
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,960
How long have you been at your present address?

38
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:11,340
Er, is it more than two years?

39
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,028
Ah, just two weeks actually.

40
00:01:13,028 --> 00:01:16,067
I only arrived in the country a month ago.

41
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:17,080
I'm from Holland.

42
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:17,390
Oh,

43
00:01:17,390 --> 00:01:18,010
that's fine.

44
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:21,420
But we normally ask for a previous address in that case.

45
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:27,738
Oh yes, well, it's Rielsdorf 2.

46
00:01:27,738 --> 00:01:31,950
That's R-I-E-L-S-D-O-R-F 2, Utrecht.

47
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:32,539
Holland.

48
00:01:32,539 --> 00:01:33,128
OK.

49
00:01:33,128 --> 00:01:34,306
Thank you.

50
00:01:34,306 --> 00:01:38,430
Do you have a daytime telephone number?

51
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:43,147
Yes, I think the number at my office is six-oh-six-two-nine-five.

52
00:01:43,147 --> 00:01:46,449
Um, just a minute, I'd better check.

53
00:01:46,449 --> 00:01:48,808
Oh no sorry, six- one-six.

54
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:51,638
I'm not used to it yet.

55
00:01:51,638 --> 00:01:54,940
Would you like my home number too?

56
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:57,490
Yes please.

57
00:01:57,490 --> 00:02:00,040
It's seven-nine-six-four-three-one.

58
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:02,365
Are they both local numbers?

59
00:02:02,365 --> 00:02:02,830
Yes.

60
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:04,032
Right.

61
00:02:04,032 --> 00:02:07,640
And your occupation?

62
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,469
Well, I'm in Britain as a project manager,

63
00:02:10,469 --> 00:02:12,592
but that's not my main job.

64
00:02:12,592 --> 00:02:14,360
I'm an engineer by profession.

65
00:02:14,360 --> 00:02:15,038
I see.

66
00:02:15,038 --> 00:02:17,071
I think I'll put that then.

67
00:02:17,071 --> 00:02:17,749
It's shorter!

68
00:02:17,749 --> 00:02:22,493
Now we usually ask for a piece of information which we can use to

69
00:02:22,493 --> 00:02:24,527
check your identity, for security reasons.

70
00:02:24,527 --> 00:02:26,560
You know, if you phone us.

71
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,960
Like, erm, my wife's first name?

72
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,392
Mother's might be better.

73
00:02:30,392 --> 00:02:32,540
It's less likely to be known.

74
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:33,324
OK.

75
00:02:33,324 --> 00:02:35,678
Hers is Siti.

76
00:02:35,678 --> 00:02:36,462
Siti?

77
00:02:36,462 --> 00:02:38,031
Yes, S-I-T-I.

78
00:02:38,031 --> 00:02:39,600
It's Indonesian.

79
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:39,968
Fine.

80
00:02:39,968 --> 00:02:44,020
And how much would you like to open your account with?

81
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:47,335
We usually ask for a minimum sum of £50.

82
00:02:47,335 --> 00:02:48,440
That's about €75.

83
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:53,413
Well, I'm going to transfer €2,000 from my Dutch account, just till I get

84
00:02:53,413 --> 00:02:53,745
paid.

85
00:02:53,745 --> 00:02:56,729
In fact, I wanted to ask you about that.

86
00:02:56,729 --> 00:02:59,050
What's the best way to do it?

87
00:02:59,050 --> 00:03:01,230
It depends which bank you're with.

88
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:03,620
It's the Fransen Bank in Utrecht.

89
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,171
OK, fine.

90
00:03:04,171 --> 00:03:05,824
I'll check that in a minute.

91
00:03:05,824 --> 00:03:09,130
If we have links with them we can do a direct transfer.

92
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:11,875
But it's not a big problem either way.

93
00:03:11,875 --> 00:03:12,905
Um, let's see.

94
00:03:12,905 --> 00:03:15,650
How often would you like to receive statements?

95
00:03:15,650 --> 00:03:17,392
I haven't really thought.

96
00:03:17,392 --> 00:03:19,570
Um, what's the usual thing?

97
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:20,663
It's up to you.

98
00:03:20,663 --> 00:03:22,030
Some people like them weekly.

99
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:22,721
Oh, no,

100
00:03:22,721 --> 00:03:23,759
that's too often.

101
00:03:23,759 --> 00:03:26,870
Can I have them sent, um, once a month?

102
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:27,276
Yes,

103
00:03:27,276 --> 00:03:28,087
that's fine.

104
00:03:28,087 --> 00:03:29,710
Is there anything else?

105
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:33,870
I was thinking of registering for your internet service at some stage.

106
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:34,559
Oh, yes.

107
00:03:34,559 --> 00:03:38,001
Would you like me to send you information about that?

108
00:03:38,001 --> 00:03:38,690
Please, yes.

109
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:43,760
And would you like to receive information about the bank's other services - insurance,

110
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,320
loans, anything like that?

111
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,400
Hmm, I don't think so, thanks.

112
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,681
That's OK then.

113
00:03:48,681 --> 00:03:51,670
And one last thing, if you agree...
